Launch from a full private view for other compatibility tools

`run --materialize-all --view-dir <dir>` writes every decrypted package
file, not only the executables, into a temporary launch view inside an
owner-only (0700) directory, so the game runs on any Wine or Proton with no
WINE_DLL_FILE_MAP or WINE_EXE_FILE_MAP and none of the runtime's memfd
loader patches. The view directory must be an absolute, non-symlinked
directory of this user with mode 0700; there is no fallback next to the game
or in /tmp. Executables keep the PE checks of the launch chain; other
encrypted files are copied as is. The decrypted memfds are closed on exec, so
Wine, Proton and the game do not inherit them, and no PlayFab token is passed
in the environment of a full view. Without the flag nothing changes,
except that every launch view directory, including the executable-only one
next to the game, is now created with mode 0700 instead of the umask's
(often 0755), so other users cannot read decrypted executables.

